To qualify for the 24-month extension, you must:

1. Have been granted OPT and currently be in a valid period of post-completion OPT;
2. Have earned a bachelor’s, master’s, or doctoral degree from a school that is accredited by a U.S. Department of Education-recognized accrediting agency and is certified by the Student and Exchange Visitor Program (SEVP) at the time you submit your STEM OPT extension application;
3. Have a STEM degree included on the current DHS STEM Designated Degree Program List;
4. Be employed by an employer who is enrolled in and is using E-Verify; and
5. Have received an initial grant of post-completion OPT employment authorization based on your STEM degree.

Additionally, if you are an F-1 student participating in a 12-month period of post-completion OPT based on a non-STEM degree, you may be eligible to use a previous STEM degree from a U.S. institution of higher education to apply for a STEM OPT extension, as long as you meet the above requirements and the practical training opportunity is directly related to the previously obtained STEM degree.
